# Nobody to ask in Russian: некого, некогда, нечего
subtitle: "Мне некогда, некого попросить, ни сын, ни дочь: say there's nobody to ask and no time, and how that differs from никто не."
tags: ["russian","некого нечего","russian negatives","birthday in russian","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/negatives","vocabulary/holidays"]
thumb: "band \"Nobody to ask in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Reading Tolstoy in Russian: The Lion and the Little Dog","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/160-russian-tolstoy.cast"}

